What interval notation is shown on this number line?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\draw[{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (-2.9,0)--(2.9,0);
\foreach \x in {-5,...,5} {\draw (0.5*\x,0.12)--(0.5*\x,-0.12); \node[below] at (0.5*\x,-0.16) {\x};}
\draw[very thick,-{Stealth}] (1,0)--(-2.7,0);
\fill (1,0) circle (2.4pt);
\node[right] at (3,0) {$x$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

What is the interval notation for a number line with an open circle at $-4$ and a closed circle at $1$, shaded between them?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\draw[{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (-3.4,0)--(2.4,0);
\foreach \x in {-6,...,4} {\draw (0.5*\x,0.12)--(0.5*\x,-0.12); \node[below] at (0.5*\x,-0.16) {\x};}
\draw[very thick] (-2,0)--(0.5,0);
\draw[fill=white] (-2,0) circle (2.4pt);
\fill (0.5,0) circle (2.4pt);
\node[right] at (2.5,0) {$x$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
